      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/burke_new_york",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Northern Ogdensburg Railroad opened a station in Burke in 1850, linking the town to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/burke_new_york",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Little Trout River winds northwest through Burke, feeding the larger Trout River watershed that reaches Quebec.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
